{{Quote|Mos Eisley Spaceport. You will never find a more wretched hive of scum and villainy. We must be cautious.|Obi-Wan Kenobi, to Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
'''Mos Eisley''', also known as '''Mos Eisley Spaceport''', was a large [[spaceport]] [[city|settlement]] located southeast of the [[Jundland Wastes]] on the backwater [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. Cratered with 362 [[Hangar|docking bays]], many of which were large enough to accommodate [[freighter]]s, Mos Eisley was an epicenter of [[Smuggler|smuggling]] operations in the Outer Rim and as such served as a safe haven for [[spacers]], [[scoundrel]]s, and rogues alike no matter their [[species]] or buissness. As a result, city and customs officials were notoriously open to bribes and did little to curtail the rampant smuggling operations that passed through the city, leading to the city gaining infamy of being a hive of scum and villainy, which the settlement prided itself on. As such, local [[farmer]]s only brought their harvests to the shady settlement if markets in Tatooine's [[capital]] [[Bestine (city)|Bestine]] were overly busy.

==Description==
[[File:MosEisleyFarFarAway-ANH.jpg|left|thumb|270x270px|Mos Eisley as seen from the Junland Wastes]]
Mos Eisley was a [[spaceport]] [[city|settlement]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]]<ref name="Ultimate" /> home to various [[species]] of aliens from throughout [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> It was located in a broad valley<ref name="CL" /> in the [[Great Mesra Plateau]], north of [[Anchorhead]] and southeast of the [[Jundland Wastes]]. The spaceport, while lacking a primary landing facility, contained 362 [[hangar]]s in which arrivals could berth.<ref name="Ultimate" /> The city was roughly divided into the [[Old Quarter]],<ref name="Altaya" /> which was laid out like a wheel surrounding the [[water distribution plant]], and the new city center adjacent to the [[Mos Eisley prefecture militia base]]. On the far side of the city was [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] and the [["Community" junk yard]].<ref name="CL" />

[[File:Ubrikkian_Trade_Tower.png|thumb|240x240px|The Ubrikkian Trade Tower, one of the tallest buildings in Mos Eisley]]
The Old Quarter was roughly defined by [[Outer Curved Street]] and [[Inner Curved Street]], and included [[Spacers Row]] and [[Paradise Road]]. Besides the water and power distribution plants around which it was arranged, the Quarter was filled with small landing bays, stores and the city market, while in later years various off-world corporations contributed to its gentrification by constructing larger buildings including the [[Ubrikkian Trade Tower]] and the [[Quebe-Luxfause Systems headquarters]]. The city's [[Spaceport prefect's office|prefecture]] and [[Spaceport Traffic Control]] offices were also located there, as was the [[Customs House]]. An ancient [[colony ship]], the ''[[Dowager Queen]]'' lay crashed by [[Dune Street]] and was maintained as a monument.<ref name="CL" />

Upwards from [[Kerner Plaza]] and towards the far end of [[Straight Street]] was the new city center, which was marked by newer buildings including the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] prefecture base and a [[Dim-U monastery]]. This area of Mos Eisley was dominated by [[hotel]]s, [[casino]]s and tall complexes built by off-world companies.<ref name="CL" />

==History==
[[File:JabbatheHutt-SWCT.jpg|left|thumb|281x281px|Jabba the Hutt established a sizable presence in the city after moving there from Mos Espa]]
Some time after the [[Separatist Crisis]] [[podracing]] fell out of favor, leading many gangsters and criminals to abandon the sport's capital in the north of Tatooine, [[Mos Espa]] and seek out new prosperous grounds for exploitation. Many of them, including influential [[Hutt]] criminal [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] made their way to Mos Eisley, bringing a breath of fresh air to the city. By the time of the [[Imperial Era]], Mos Eisley had become a relatively wealthy town, attracting scum and villainy from around the planet and beyond. Jabba even had [[Desilijic Complex|an expansive townshouse complex]] built in the city's historic center and maintained a private box in the town's [[Felvath Kurs Arena]]. The [[Desilijic]] crime family had established a strong presence in the town, with Jabba's personal cook [[Porcellus]] working as the head chef on the exotic restaurant [[Court of the Fountain]]. Jabba and his empire's presence caught the attention of off-world businesses including [[Ubrikkian Industries]] and [[Quebe-Luxfause Systems]], both of which constructed high-rise buildings in the old city center, leading to the gentrification of the once-rundown neighborhood.<ref name="CL" />

With the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' parked in [[Docking Bay 94]], Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina was where [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] met [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]], during their attempts to reach [[Alderaan]] and deliver the [[Death Star plans]] to the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]]. [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s also searched Mos Eisley for [[R2-D2]] and [[C-3PO]], the holders of the missing [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] plans. The cantina was also home to the infamous confrontation between Han Solo and [[Greedo]], which led to Greedo's untimely death. [[Ponda Baba]] and Dr. [[Cornelius Evazan]] were present at Mos Eisley, and Obi-Wan Kenobi cut off Ponda Baba's right arm with his [[lightsaber]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> Shortly afterward, Kenobi and Skywalker were confronted by a [[Unidentified stormtrooper (Mos Eisley)|stormtrooper]], whom the Jedi killed.<ref name="LINE">[[Star Wars (LINE Webtoon)|''Star Wars'' LINE Webtoon]]</ref> The group escaped from Mos Eisley in the ''Falcon'' after a shootout with stormtroopers.<ref name="Episode IV" />

[[File:MosEisley-celebration.png|thumb|270x270px|Celebrations for the destruction of the second Death Star in Outer Curved Street]]
When [[Boba Fett]] was hired by [[Darth]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Vader]] to find information on the [[pilot]] who [[Battle of Yavin|destroyed]] the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], he discovered that the boy had escaped Mos Eisley on Han Solo's ship along with Kenobi. Not knowing the latter, he interrogated a gang of [[Rodian]]s, who informed him of the location of Kenobi's home in the Dune Sea.<ref name="Star Wars 4">[[Star Wars (2015) 4|''Star Wars'' (2015) 4]]</ref> To learn the name of the pilot, Fett went to Chalmun's cantina knowing that Han Solo had frequented it. There, he learned of Skywalker's name from a [[Unidentified moisture farmer (Chalmun's Cantina)|young moisture farmer]], and went in search of him, [[Duel in Ben Kenobi's home|encountering]] him in the home of Obi-Wan Kenobi.<ref name="Star Wars 5">[[Star Wars (2015) 5|''Star Wars'' (2015) 5]]</ref>

The city [[Parades on Tatooine|celebrated]] the [[Battle of Endor|destruction]] of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]] and the death of the [[Darth Sidious|Emperor]].<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Boba Fett visited the city to meet with a [[Pyke]] [[Pyke Boss|boss]] in the [[Desert Survey Office]].<ref name="Streets" />

[[File:Stormtrooper_helmet_pikes.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Stormtrooper helmets on pikes in Mos Eisley.]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|5}}</ref> the [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] arrived in Mos Eisley looking for repairs to his ship, the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', and took a job with [[Toro Calican]] to [[Hunt for Fennec Shand|hunt]] [[Fennec Shand]]. Toro shot her and left her for dead on the sands of Tatooine.<ref name="The Mandalorian Chapter 5">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 5: The Gunslinger}}</ref> Shortly after, Boba Fett found her, and took her to a [[Mos Eisley Mod Parlor|mod-parlor]], where a [[The Modifier|modifier]] saved her life.<ref name="Gathering Storm" />

Djarin later returned to Mos Eisley in in search of a Mandalorian to help him, and proceeded to [[Freetown|Mos Pelgo]], where he met [[Cobb Vanth]].<ref name="The Mandalorian Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref><ref name="The Mandalorian Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref> He later returned to the city, and was introduced to "[[Frog Lady]]" by Peli, who said she might know where to find Mandalorians.<ref name="The Mandalorian Chapter 10" /> After the destruction of the ''Razor Crest'', Djarin returned to Peli again, and she helped him to modify an [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|N-1 starfighter]].<ref name="BOBF Chapter 5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>

During the [[Battle of Mos Espa|Battle for Mos Espa]], Fennec Shand [[Assassination of the Pyke Syndicate leaders|assassinated]] the Pyke Boss and his partners in the [[Desert Survey Office]] in the outskirts of the town.<ref name="BOBF Chapter 7">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>

==Government==
[[File:Mos_Eisley_street.png|thumb|220x220px|The Prefect's office on Straight Street, guarded by two stormtroopers (left)]]
During the Imperial Era, Mos Eisley was ruled as a prefecture, under an [[Prefect (Galactic Empire)|Imperial prefect]] who had an office<ref name="CL" /> guarded by [[stormtrooper]]s in the Old Quarter. The local militia base acted as a garrison, guarding the city, maintaining foot patrols and establishing checkpoints.<ref name="Episode IV" />

